INSERT INTO public.exam_questions (subject_id,subject_name,year,position,text,options,answer,explanation) VALUES
(5,'Biology','2017',41,'Two women were decided not to have pregnancy in the near future and they were offered two different contraceptive options. In woman I, the material fitted in her uterus did not allow the sperm to fertilize the egg. In woman II, the contraceptive prevented hormone production and the releasing of eggs from the ovaries. Which type of contraceptive methods did woman I and II used, respectively?','["Sterilization and Injectable contraceptives Depo-Provera", "Post pill and copper-coated intrauterine device", "Contraceptive injection and contraceptive implant", "Copper-coated intrauterine device and contraceptive injection"]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',42,'The finding of the study conducted in two different villages showed that there are harmful practices that affect reproductive health. The common practices in village 1 were forcing underage girls to get married based on norms and sexual abuse or harassment. In village 2, abduction to make the girl a wife unwillingly was very common. Which one of the following options is correct about the two villages?','["In village 1, gender-based violence, kidnapping and female genital mutilation are common.", "In village 1, gender-based violence and early marriage are common.", "In village 2, kidnapping and female genital mutilation are common.", "In village 2, gender-based violence and female genital mutilation are common."]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',43,'How does drinking alcohol contribute to HIV transmission? By','["improving the decision making ability of a person", "driving more willingly to participate in risky behaviors", "impotency or loss of sexual drive both in male and female", "increasing rate of the retrovirus multiplication capacity"]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',44,'Select the option where the whole list contains renewable natural resources.','["Coal, oil, natural gas and minerals", "Coal, wind, hydro power and biomass", "Sunlight, wind, hydro power and biomass", "Sunlight, wind, hydro power and natural gas"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',45,'This item is based on the following list of activities. I. Establishing national parks II. Wild sanctuaries III. Preparing wild life reserves IV. Practicing overgrazing Which of the above activities CANNOT be used for the conservation of wild life?','["II", "I", "III", "IV"]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',46,'Among the following options, identify the air pollutants that can cause acid rain and its effects, respectively.','["Carbon dioxide and methane - melting of ice caps and rising of oceans", "Sulphur dioxides and nitrogen dioxides - damaging plants and water", "Perflourocarbons - causing skin cancer and cataracts", "Chloroflourocarbons - increasing UV rays and respiratory disease"]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',47,'Which of the following is the cause and effect of global warming, respectively?','["Greenhouse gases and dropping of sea levels", "Greenhouse gases and loss of biodiversity", "Burning of fossil fuels and increase in species diversity", "Burning of fossil fuels and dropping of sea level"]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',48,'What is the primary purpose of creating transgenic organisms? To','["generate pathogenic organisms that fight against non-pathogenic ones", "produce organisms that mimic human beings in every aspect of behaviors", "promote expression of desired genes that improve nutritional quality of organisms", "produce novel organisms that can affect reproduction across different species"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',49,'What is the role of biology in the investigation of a criminal case? To','["detect flavor compounds in food and monitor environmental pollutants", "examine potential sources of evidences using blood, saliva and hair", "sense pathogens and herbicides using immunochemical detection system", "determine the production of complex organic compounds using mold fungus"]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',50,'How does biological washing powder save energy? Because they','["use lipase enzyme without other combination for any stain in clothes.", "are effective in cleaning clothes at lower temperatures without boiling water.", "are effective in removing dirty ores in clothes without spraying acidic water.", "use protease enzyme without other combination for any stain in clothes."]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',51,'What is biological warfare? The use of','["selective genes to produce genetically modified organisms", "cloning technique to make exact genetic copies of an organism", "bacteria, fungi and viruses as a biological agent to control pests", "infectious agents with the intent to kill humans, animals or plants"]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',52,'Which of the following correctly describes the general features of bacteria? They are unicellular microbes with','["true nucleus and are omnipresent in nature.", "rigid cell wall and a diverse mode of nutrition.", "mitochondria and a special type of chlorophyll.", "Golgi bodies and genetic materials of a cell."]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',53,'Which group of archaea are found in volcanic vents and hot vapors that contain either obligate aerobes, facultative aerobes or obligate anaerobes?','["Hyperthermophiles", "Acidophiles", "Halophiles", "Psychrophiles"]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',54,'From the fungal diseases given below, which one is transmitted sexually?','["Candidiasis", "Aspergillosis", "Tineas", "Dermatophytosis"]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',55,'This item is based on the following choices of feeding habit employed by organisms. I. Using nutrients dissolved in the surrounding medium II. Manufacturing own nutrients by photosynthesis III. Depending on other plants or animals for food Which method/s do protozoans use to get their nutrition? They employed','["I only.", "I and II only.", "II and III only.", "I, II and III."]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',56,'Which one of the following diseases is correctly matched with its symptoms and method of transmission?','["Chickenpox - runny and stuffy nose - respiratory droplets", "Measles - paralysis and hydrophobia - bite from infected animals", "Polio - commonly no sign and symptoms - fecal-oral-route", "Rabies - swollen and painful protid glands - through infected saliva"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',57,'In order to link a specific microorganism to a specific disease, Koch used mouse as experimental animal. He took a small amount of blood from a diseased mouse and injected into a healthy mouse, the latter quickly developed anthrax. Again he took blood from this second mouse and then injected it into another, again he observed the symptoms of anthrax. What was his first postulate related with this procedure?','["The same microorganisms are present in every case of the diseases.", "The isolated microorganisms can cause the same disease to susceptible animal.", "The same pathogens are isolated and re-cultivated from experimental animal.", "The microorganisms are isolated from the tissue of a dead animal and pure culture is prepared."]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',58,'Sleeping sickness is transmitted by','["biting of tsetse flies.", "sexual intercourse.", "eating contaminated food.", "droplet infection."]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',59,'Considering the diverse application of microorganisms, which of the following best evaluates their overall importance? They have','["abundant benefits that are essential for life on Earth.", "a great disadvantage and limited advantage.", "limited impact on the environment.", "few applications in the areas of biotechnology and medicine."]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',60,'Suppose a clinical nurse used a needle to treat a person with HIV/AIDS. What would be the most appropriate method of controlling such microbial infection?','["Incineration", "Tyndallization", "Sanitization", "Preservation"]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',61,'As a clinical microbiologist, suppose you want to collect microbes from a food sample and isolate them via serial dilution. How do you determine the isolated colonies that grow on artificial media?','["counting the number of strains on the plate", "cross checking with other preserved specimens", "observing their morphological features", "inoculating them into other infected animals"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',62,'What is the main difference between anabolism and catabolism in cellular metabolic pathways? Anabolism','["absorbs energy while catabolism releases energy.", "is destructive while catabolism is constructive process.", "occurs during respiration while catabolism occurs in photosynthesis.", "breaks down macromolecules while catabolism buildups them."]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',63,'In a hypothetical scenario where photosynthesis ceased to occur on the earth, the long-term consequences on the continuity of life would be','["remained unaffected since other sources of energy exist.", "collapsed that could lead to mass extinction.", "balanced between CO2 and O2 appropriately.", "disordered although animal life would flourish."]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',64,'What are the roles of grana and stroma in the process of photosynthesis? Grana is a site for','["cyclic pathway while stroma is a site for non-cyclic pathway.", "photolysis of water while stroma is a site for carbon fixation.", "generation of sugar while stroma is a site for photolysis of water.", "production of NADPH while stroma is a site for chemiosmosis."]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',65,'Which one of the following comparisons between cyclic and non-cyclic photophosphorylation is correct? Non-cyclic photophosphorylation','["produces ATP, NADPH and O2, but cyclic produces ATP and NADPH.", "uses oxygen as the final electron acceptor, but cyclic uses cytochrome b-c1 complex.", "uses photosystem I as electron donor, but cyclic uses water as an electron donor.", "involves both photosystems I and II, but cyclic uses only photosystem I."]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',66,'All of the following events happen in the reduction stages of the Calvin cycle EXCEPT','["combining of CO2 with RuBP.", "utilization of ATP and NADPH molecules.", "conversion of 3-PGA into a sugar molecule.", "donating of electrons to a 3C-intermediates to form G3P."]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',67,'What happens in the mitochondrion during the reactions of photorespiration?','["Glycine is converted to serine with the release of CO2 and NH3.", "Glycolate is converted to glyoxylate with the release of H2O2.", "Glycerate is converted to GP with the release of ADP.", "Phosphoglycolate is converted to glycolate with the release of Pi"]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',68,'How does photosynthesis ensure the continuity of life? By','["constantly adding carbon dioxide to the atmosphere", "maintaining carbon dioxide and oxygen balance in the atmosphere", "constantly removing oxygen from the atmosphere", "adding natural gas and absorbing methane from the atmosphere"]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',69,'Which of the following is the difference between substrate level phosphorylation and oxidative phosphorylation? Substrate level phosphorylation','["occurs in the inner mitochondrial membrane while oxidative phosphorylation occurs in the cytosol.", "occurs during glycolysis and Kreb''s cycle while oxidative phosphorylation occurs during electron transport chain.", "has the same source of energy as oxidative phosphorylation.", "occurs in aerobic respiration while oxidative phosphorylation in anaerobic respiration."]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',70,'Which one of the following is correct about the energy liberation phase of glycolysis pathway? It','["hydrolyses two ATP molecules and raises the free energy of glucose.", "breaks six carbon molecules into two glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate molecules.", "releases one water molecule and dihydroxyacetone phosphate molecule.", "produces four ATP, two NADH and two molecules of pyruvate."]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',71,'Which one of the following statements describes an event of the process of electron transport system correctly?','["Oxygen serves as a terminal electron acceptor in the production of ATP.", "Thirteen ATP molecules are invested when electrons are transferred from NADH/FADH2 to O2.", "More than 90% of the total ATP is produced by substrate-level phosphorylation.", "It happens due to the difference in pH as the inside mitochondrial membrane is more acidic."]'::jsonb,0,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',72,'In a complete oxidation of glucose molecule, how many net ATP molecules are produced by substrate level phosphorylation?','["2", "4", "8", "10"]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',73,'What is the difference between aerobic and anaerobic respirations?','["Aerobic respiration ends with different products while the same product results in anaerobic respiration.", "Proteins are the main respiratory substrate for both aerobic and anaerobic respiration.", "Aerobic respiration produces much more energy than anaerobic respiration.", "Glycolysis is the first pathway for aerobic while Kreb''s cycle is for anaerobic respiration."]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',74,'Which one of the following statements disproves spontaneous generation theory based on a step wise experimental work?','["Life is an inherent property of the universe and everlasting.", "Different life forms on the Earth were created by a supreme being within six days.", "Both macro and micro-organisms could arise from pre-existing organisms.", "Life has reached to the Earth in the form of spores with falling meteorite."]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',75,'Based on comparative anatomy, chimpanzee is the closest relative to humans because of the similarities in their','["haemoglobin sequence.", "fossil remains.", "DNA sequence.", "pentadactyl limb."]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',76,'Which one of the following causes of variation allows infertile hybrids to become fertile in plant evolution?','["Reproductive isolation", "Sympatric speciation", "Polyploidy cell", "Geographical separation"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',77,'This item is based on the following course of human evolution. 1. Use of fire and other tools 2. Increase in brain size 3. Emergence of Homo sapiens 4. Bipedal walking and arboreal life Which of the following is the correct order of the above evolutionary time line markers?','["2, 1, 3, 4", "1, 3, 4, 2", "3, 2, 4, 1", "4, 2, 1, 3"]'::jsonb,3,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',78,'Which of the following is NOT a common cause of genetic mutation?','["Exposure to ultra-violet radiation", "Errors in DNA replication", "Extensive physical exercise", "Experiences of using chemical substance"]'::jsonb,2,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',79,'Which genetic phenomenon is common for both bottleneck and founder effects?','["High mutation rate that enhances adaptation", "Genetic drift that reduces diversity in the population", "Gene flow that increases inbreed and disease''s resistance", "Natural selection that results from gradual evolutionary changes"]'::jsonb,1,''),
(5,'Biology','2017',80,'In a scenario where a male black lion population left its terrestrial territory and joined a white female lion population in an isolated Island to mate, there would be a','["decrease in black lion population in the isolated Island.", "genetic variation in terrestrial population due to immigration.", "random introduction of new alleles into the Island population.", "change in allele frequencies of terrestrial population but not in Island."]'::jsonb,2,'');